{"abstract":[{"text":"How the default placeholders’ built-in text is localized, how to add a language, and how to show different text instead without touching ScreenStates itself.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/localization"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Localization","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Localization","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"],"title":"Related Documentation"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Loading\/Error placeholders’ text — “Nothing Here,” “Loading,” “Retry,” “Something Went Wrong,” “Connection Issue” — comes from a String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":", resolved from ScreenStates’ own bundle ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle.module"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than your app’s. That’s deliberate: a custom title your app passes in (see below) is never run back through localization, and a language you add to "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"your own","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" app’s catalog has no effect on these five strings — they only ever resolve against ScreenStates’ bundle. English, Spanish, French, and Russian are built in today."}]},{"text":"Adding a language to ScreenStates","type":"heading","anchor":"Adding-a-language-to-ScreenStates","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a change to the package itself, not something a consuming app can do on its own — it needs a PR. Open "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" and add a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizations"},{"type":"text","text":" entry for the new language code under each of the five string keys:"}]},{"syntax":"json","type":"codeListing","code":["\"Retry\" : {","  \"comment\" : \"Title of the button that retries loading after an error.\",","  \"localizations\" : {","    \"en\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Retry\" } },","    \"de\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Wiederholen\" } }","  }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every one of the five keys needs an entry for every language — a string present in English but missing a translation elsewhere fails CI (see below). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStatesStrings.swift"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s doc comments list all five keys and their English text if you’re starting from scratch."}]},{"text":"Overriding text per-app","type":"heading","anchor":"Overriding-text-per-app","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You don’t need a new language, or a PR, to show different text than the built-in default — two options, depending on how much you want to replace:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"type":"text","text":" directly, bypassing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" entirely for that one string. Pass your own localized string (from your own app’s String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSLocalizedString"},{"type":"text","text":", whatever) instead of the default:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title: String(localized: \"No Results\"))"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView"},{"type":"text","text":" has no equivalent for its title or Retry button text today — only the error’s own message is customizable, via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For anything else — the Error placeholder’s title, the Retry button’s text, or any text at all in a shape the built-in views don’t expose a parameter for — pass a fully custom placeholder instead of the default one, via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"empty"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loading"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" builder closures (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"‘s equivalent. A custom placeholder can still reuse "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" so VoiceOver announces transitions with the same wording your custom text uses, instead of the default’s."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateViewController":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIViewController"},{"type":"text","text":" base class that owns a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pinned to the view’s edges and bound to a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wrapping the boilerplate every UIKit screen using ScreenStates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise repeats in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"viewDidLoad()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstateviewcontroller","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateViewController","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScreenStateViewController","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateViewController","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give any screen a standard "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Empty"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Loading"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" state, usable from both UIKit and SwiftUI."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates","type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"ScreenStates"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI":{"abstract":[{"text":"Drive a SwiftUI screen’s four states with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithswiftui","title":"Getting Started with SwiftUI","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateView":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Renders the right content for a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", switching between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Empty \/ Loading \/ Data \/ Error automatically."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstateview","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateView","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScreenStateView","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateView","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateContainerView":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIView"},{"type":"text","text":" that swaps its content for the right placeholder based on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"type":"text","text":", mirroring "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":" from the SwiftUI side."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatecontainerview","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateContainerView","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScreenStateContainerView","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateContainerView","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" holder of a screen’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"text":", driving both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI and UIKit consumers from a single source of truth.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateStore"}],"title":"ScreenStateStore","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateStore"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four canonical states of a screen: nothing to show yet, in flight,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"showing data, or failed."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenState","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScreenState","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenState","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithUIKit":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drive a UIKit screen’s four states with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithuikit","title":"Getting Started with UIKit","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/Accessibility":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything the default placeholders — and your own custom ones — get for free: VoiceOver, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type, and stable identifiers for XCUITest."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/accessibility","title":"Accessibility","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState/accessibilityAnnouncement":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The same text the default placeholders announce to VoiceOver for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this case, reusable by a fully custom placeholder that wants to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"announce transitions with the same wording instead of inventing its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":", since at that point a custom placeholder’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own content is what VoiceOver should read, not a transition"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"announcement."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate\/accessibilityannouncement","title":"accessibilityAnnouncement","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"accessibilityAnnouncement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateDisplayableError":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Lets an error type supply its own user-facing message, distinct from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizedDescription"},{"type":"text","text":" — which is often a debugging string (or, for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStringConvertible"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedError"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conformance, just the type name) rather than something to put in front"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the person using the app."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatedisplayableerror","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","kind":"identifier"}]}}}